{
  "$schema": "./crawlers.schema.json",
  "version": "2026-09-19",
  "notes": [
    "This file is DATA, not code. Edit it, ship it, or host it and point the",
    "middleware at it with `catalog.url`. Nothing here is hardcoded in the engine.",
    "",
    "`verification.methods` is an ordered list. The engine tries each in order:",
    "  dns  - reverse DNS on the client IP, then forward-confirm the PTR hostname",
    "         back to that same IP. Only useful when the operator actually",
    "         publishes PTR records; a wrong suffix here causes false 'spoofed'.",
    "  cidr - client IP must fall inside a published prefix list. `ranges` is",
    "         checked first; `rangesUrl` is only fetched when the middleware is",
    "         started with `fetchRanges: true` (off by default, no surprise egress).",
    "A method that says 'not this operator' is a negative; a method that cannot",
    "answer (no ranges loaded, DNS timeout) is inconclusive. Verified beats",
    "negative beats inconclusive.",
    "",
    "Crawlers with `verification.methods: []` have no published way to verify them.",
    "They are detected and logged, but their identity claim is never confirmed, so",
    "they resolve to the `onUnknown` policy action. Do not invent suffixes to make",
    "that number go down - a false suffix blocks real crawlers.",
    "",
    "`robotsOnly: true` means the token is a robots.txt opt-out control, not a",
    "user-agent string. Google-Extended and Applebot-Extended never appear in a",
    "User-Agent header; they govern how an already-crawled page may be used. They",
    "show up in generated robots.txt and in the dashboard toggles, and are never",
    "matched against request traffic."
  ],
